  "hints": [
    "Each key needs a use count. Evicting means finding the lowest count, and among those the key used longest ago.",
    "Group keys by count: one ordered bucket per frequency, plus a map from key to its value and count. A hit moves the key from bucket f to bucket f + 1.",
    "Track minFreq, the lowest non-empty count. A new key resets it to 1; when a hit empties bucket minFreq, minFreq goes up by one. In each bucket, a Map's insertion order is the recency order."
  ],
  "complexity": {"time":"O(1) for get and put","space":"O(capacity)"}
